  "Number": 4,
  "Question": "It takes Mary \\(30\\) minutes to walk uphill \\(1\\) km from her home to school, but it takes her only \\(10\\) minutes to walk from school to home along the same route. What is her average speed, in km/hr, for the round trip?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(3\\)",
    "B": "\\(3.125\\)",
    "C": "\\(3.5\\)",
    "D": "\\(4\\)",
    "E": "\\(4.5\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Average speed is total distance divided by total time. The same route is \\(1\\) km each way, so Mary's round-trip distance is \\(2\\) km. Her total walking time is\n\\[\n30+10=40\\text{ minutes}=\\frac{40}{60}=\\frac23\\text{ hour}.\n\\]\nThus her average speed is\n\\[\n\\frac{2}{2/3}=3\\text{ km/hr}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{3\\text{ km/hr}}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
